  "result": "Fixed in `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. `shlex` treats `#` as a comment start by default, so everything from the `#` onward was dropped from the completion line. I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is an ordinary character.\n\n`split_arg_string('ex a#b #c')` now returns `['ex', 'a#b', '#c']`, and the shell completion tests pass (58 passed). I didn't add a regression test for the `#` case.",
